import_caveat (recorded honestly): the package uses a src/ layout and the
  checkout is not pip-installed, so `import exceptiongroup` inside the test
  run resolves the exceptiongroup already installed in the environment
  (a pytest dependency on Python < 3.11), not src/. Running with
  PYTHONPATH=src fails at import (ModuleNotFoundError:
  exceptiongroup._version — the _version module is generated by
  setuptools_scm at install time). The declared benchmark protocol is
  therefore the plain `python3 -m pytest -q` run from the repo root in the
  pinned environment; all atom propositions are phrased operationally
  against that command, and all recorded outcomes were actually observed.
